<title>UK: SOCCER-STRUGGLING OLDHAM NAME NEW MANAGER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-STRUGGLING OLDHAM NAME NEW MANAGER.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Struggling English first division side Oldham appointed former Plymouth boss Neil Warnock as their new manager on Friday.</p>
<p>Warnock took over from Graeme Sharp, who was sacked with Oldham anchored at the bottom of the table.</p>
</text>
